<title>HONG KONG: Bouygues wins US$92 mln China contract.</title>
<headline>Bouygues wins US$92 mln China contract.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bouygues Shanghai, a subsidiary of French construction company Bouygues, said on Wednesday it has won a US$92 million contract to be the main contractor for a 55-storey office tower in Shanghai.</p>
<p>Shanghai Maxdo Centre, with a total floor area of 132,800 square metres, is scheduled for completion in June 1998, Bouygues Shanghai said in a statement.</p>
<p>The basement and ground floor have already been completed under a separate contract, it said.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6590</p>
</text>
